  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186172130,
      "id": "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632",
      "title": "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7d206b38-df94-5588-845c-04813c06e146",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x - y^{2} z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u v,\\,- u,\\,3 u - v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3 u - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,-1,\\,3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3 u - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,- 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 v & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 u & 0 & - 2 v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & - 2 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 v & 3 \\\\ 2 u & - 2 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 v & -1 \\\\ 2 u & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,6 u + 4 v^{2},\\,2 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2 v,\\,6 u + 4 v^{2},\\,2 u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2 v)^{2}+(6 u + 4 v^{2})^{2}+(2 u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x - y^{2} z)\\,{|}_{x=2 u v\\,y=- u\\,z=3 u - v^{2}} \\\\  & =2 u v-1\\cdot (- u)^{2}\\cdot (3 u - v^{2}) \\\\  & =- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "27483cd1-fc63-57b7-82c5-fd8540038450",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "bf0da7f6-74c9-595e-935f-fa2d5e17164f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\left(- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\sqrt{40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "9c93004a-cd83-5a5e-91b3-6afd517b9553",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\left(- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v\\right) \\left(40 u^{2} + 48 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 4 v^{2}\\right)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "fdb763ec-517c-56ab-a78d-f970a030bcd1",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- 3 u^{3} + u^{2} v^{2} + 2 u v"
            },
