  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186172130,
      "id": "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632",
      "title": "Constructing Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3b4808cc-728c-55b7-90f8-734ae2943c4e",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=3 x - y^{2} z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u v,\\,- 3 u,\\,2 u - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,-3,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 v & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 u & 0 & - 4 v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2 v & 2 \\\\ 2 u & - 4 v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 v & -3 \\\\ 2 u & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12 v,\\,4 u + 8 v^{2},\\,6 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨12 v,\\,4 u + 8 v^{2},\\,6 u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(12 v)^{2}+(4 u + 8 v^{2})^{2}+(6 u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(3 x - y^{2} z)\\,{|}_{x=2 u v\\,y=- 3 u\\,z=2 u - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =6 u v-1\\cdot (- 3 u)^{2}\\cdot (2 u - 2 v^{2}) \\\\  & =- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "db2fc28a-c600-58d0-b8a2-e9ebeb14d152",
